title: Cornered — the exit obeys the world, silence remains
story: ides-of-march
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: The poet's jest answer ends with him quitting the scene —
  legal while the tiring-house door can be opened. Behind a locked
  door the world refuses the exit: the row is withheld whole and the
  default evasion stands, because silence is the one move that can
  never be taken away.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/ides-of-march/chord/ides-of-march.story
    stories/ides-of-march/tests/transcripts/cornered.transcript

---

> north
[OK: contains "Stage"]

> west
[OK: contains "Tiring-House"]

> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "The new hired man"]

# Fresh scene, first topic: the plain book row, question on its heels.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "So it is not carried"]

# The jest answer serves and he quits the scene — the exit is legal.
> ask shakespeare about a spy
[OK: contains "given in jest"]

# Now turn the key on the only door out of this room.
> take the key
[OK: contains "Taken"]

> close the door
[OK: contains "close"]

> lock the door with the key
[OK: contains "lock"]

# Re-open the talk and re-open the question behind a locked door.
> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "acknowledges you with the pen"]

> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "So it is not carried"]

# The same answer that walked him out is now refused whole by the
# world — the default evasion stands in its place.
> ask shakespeare about a spy
[OK: contains "I don't know anything about that"]
[OK: not contains "given in jest"]
